            "text": "She struggled to her feet as the world swirled around her.\nShe felt instantly sick and bent over to vomit.\nThen she started to walk. She had no idea which direction she was going. The pain in her left hip was excruciating and she kept stumbling to her knees. Each time an even greater pain shot through her head.\nShe didn’t know how long she’d been walking when she saw a light out of the corner of her eye. She changed direction. It was only when she was standing by the woodshed in the yard that she realized she had walked straight back to Zalachenko’s farmhouse. She swayed like a drunk.",
            "paragraph_end": 75,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "75c677c1a011cbe0de73878eabc8414e0a9a8990bba560a3bf6d2d4e150779b1",
            "id": "75c677c1-a011-cbe0-de73-878eabc8414e",
